# Frontend rules — artifact-hub

Always:
- Use functional components with explicit TypeScript props interfaces
- Reuse existing CSS classes from src/index.css — do NOT add Tailwind or new CSS frameworks
- Use CSS variables already defined (:root tokens like --bg-panel, --accent-function)
- Keep data fetching in src/api/client.ts — components call api helpers, never raw fetch() inline
- Use useAuth() from AuthContext for auth state — do not duplicate token logic in components
- Reuse validation from src/utils/validation.ts for form fields
- Preserve accessibility: aria-invalid, aria-describedby, role="alert" on form errors
- Match existing component patterns (LoginScreen, ArtifactHub, TitleBar)

Never:
- Introduce styled-components, MUI, or shadcn unless explicitly asked
- Store auth tokens outside src/api/client.ts helpers
- Hardcode artifact card data in components — use src/data/artifacts.ts or API types
